        <tr><td>JIS N150</td><td><a href="/data/n150/">N150 (145G51)</a></td><td>160 Ah · 1050 A (SAE −18°C ref)</td><td>Japanese &amp; European heavy trucks, buses</td></tr>
        <tr><td>JIS N200</td><td><a href="/data/n200/">N200 (190H52)</a></td><td>200 Ah · 1100 A (SAE −18°C ref)</td><td>Heavy trucks, semi-trailers, high-load buses</td></tr>
        <tr><td>JIS N100</td><td><a href="/data/n100/">N100 (95E41)</a></td><td>100 Ah · 740 A (SAE −18°C ref)</td><td>Light/medium trucks, buses</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="note">
      Capacity and CCA are reference values from this site's model database — confirm final values
      with the manufacturer. Group-to-vehicle mapping is a third-party fitment reference, a
      compatible reference rather than an OEM confirmation. DIN88/DIN100 codes serve European
      vehicles where the original fitment uses that code; Dingwei covers the DIN/EN family (see the
      <a href="/knowledge/jis-vs-din-vs-bci/">standards comparison</a>). Confirm dimensions, terminal
      layout and voltage against the specific truck before ordering.
    </p>

    <h2>Standards</h2>
    <p>
      Two standards run side by side. JIS N-series batteries (N150/N200/N100) serve the Japanese
      and Korean truck base — and, in the Middle East, most European trucks are also specified in
      the N150/N200 group by independent fitment references. DIN/EN batteries cover European
      vehicles where the original fitment uses that code. Match the battery to the vehicle's group,
      dimensions and terminal orientation rather than to the region alone. For a technical
      comparison of the standards, see
      <a href="/knowledge/jis-vs-din-vs-bci/">JIS vs DIN vs BCI</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Entry conformity is mandatory. Saudi Arabia requires SASO conformity assessment through the
      SABER electronic platform, producing a Product Certificate of Conformity (PCoC) and a
      per-shipment Shipment Certificate (SCoC) for customs clearance
      (<a href="https://www.trade.gov/saudi-arabia-testing-inspection-and-certification" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ITA / trade.gov</a>;
      <a href="https://www.gso.org.sa/en" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GSO</a>).
      Gulf-wide, the G-Mark under the Gulf Technical Regulation for Low Voltage Electrical
      Equipment applies. Confirm the current scheme, labelling and notified certification body with
      your importer before production, because post-arrival certification is slow and costly.
    </p>

    <h2>Dingwei relevance</h2>
    <p>
      Dingwei — manufactured by Chengguang Power Tech Co., Ltd. — carries the JIS N-series groups
      that dominate the Saudi fleet in one line: N150 (145G51), N200 (190H52) and N100 (95E41), and
      covers the DIN/EN family for European vehicles. These are positioned as
      <strong>compatible references</strong> matched by group, dimensions and CCA — not as OEM
      replacements — so a distributor can cover a mixed Japanese/European fleet from a single
      manufacturer and a single shipment. Dingwei does not publish a country-specific Saudi
      distributor list; supply is arranged per order with SASO/SABER conformity and final
      specifications confirmed before production.
    </p>

    <h2>Buyer considerations</h2>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Match the battery to the vehicle, not the country.</strong> Confirm group size, physical dimensions, terminal orientation and system voltage (many Saudi heavy trucks are 24V — two 12V batteries in series) against the specific unit.</li>
      <li><strong>Budget for heat-shortened life.</strong> High ambient temperatures reduce service life, so a thick-plate flooded design or sealed AGM and a disciplined electrolyte/test schedule are worth more in Riyadh and Dammam than in temperate markets.</li>
      <li><strong>Clear conformity before shipment.</strong> SASO/SABER (PCoC + SCoC) and the GCC G-Mark gate customs clearance; confirm the current scheme and labelling with your importer.</li>
      <li><strong>Plan the port.</strong> Jeddah Islamic Port serves the western region on the Red Sea Asia-Europe lane; King Abdulaziz Port Dammam serves the eastern/Arabian Gulf side. Choose the entry point nearest your distribution centre.</li>
    </ol>

